---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import TicketLink from '../../components/TicketLink.astro';
import FestivalAbc from '../../components/FestivalAbc.astro';
import { festival } from '../../config';
---

<Base title="FAQ & Festival A to Z" description="Frequently asked questions about Straussi Festival 2027: tickets, admission, getting there, food, rules – plus the Festival A to Z.">
  {/* English version of pages/faq.astro. Same structure (<details class="faq-question">, FestivalAbc). Keep both in sync.
      The A to Z is sorted by the English keywords; the letter bar adjusts automatically. */}
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>FAQ</h1>

    <h2>About the festival</h2>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>What is Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>Straussi Festival is a music festival in Stuttgart organised by three neighbouring student residences (Straussi 1, 2 and 3) that gives local student artists a stage. It takes place on four stages: a main stage with bands (mostly cover bands) and three more stages with DJs playing techno, house, trance, nu disco, bounce, dark disco and mixed party sets.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>When and where does Straussi Festival 2027 take place?</summary>
      <p>Straussi Festival 2027 takes place on 11 and 12 June 2027 on the grounds of the Straussi student residences, Universitätsstraße 94, 70569 Stuttgart, Germany.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Who is performing at Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>Most of the bands and DJs are students who live in the residences on campus – including the Straussi residences – or study at universities in Stuttgart. The festival deliberately focuses on supporting local, up-and-coming student artists. We will announce the line-up soon.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>I am an artist. Can I apply to perform?</summary>
      <p>Yes! Bands, DJs and other artists can apply by email to <a href={`mailto:${festival.emailActs}`}>{festival.emailActs}</a>.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>How many visitors does Straussi Festival expect?</summary>
      <p>Straussi Festival expects around 7,500 visitors per day.</p>
    </details>

    <h2>Tickets &amp; admission</h2>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>What tickets are there and how much do they cost?</summary>
      <p>There are <TicketLink>day tickets</TicketLink> for Friday or Saturday and <TicketLink>weekend tickets</TicketLink> for both days. All <TicketLink>ticket types</TicketLink> and prices are listed in the <TicketLink>ticket shop</TicketLink>; the “<TicketLink>Buy tickets</TicketLink>” button takes you straight there.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>When does the presale for Straussi Festival 2027 start?</summary>
      <p>The presale is already on. The “<TicketLink>Buy tickets</TicketLink>” button takes you straight to the <TicketLink>ticket shop</TicketLink>.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>How old do I have to be to attend Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>Straussi Festival is open to people <strong>aged 18 and over only</strong>. Persons under 18 will not be admitted, not even when accompanied by parents or guardians.</p>
    </details>

    <h2>Getting there &amp; on site</h2>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>What is the best way to get to Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>The best way is by S-Bahn (suburban train) to the stop Universität (lines S1, S2, S3); from there it is about a 5-minute walk to the festival site. Bus lines 82, 84, 91, 92, X74, 747, 748 and X60 also stop right at the S-Bahn station Universität. The closest stop is Schranne (about a 2-minute walk), served by lines 82, 84, 91, 92, 747, 748, N1 and X74. Map and all the ways to get here: <a href="/en/anfahrt/">Getting there</a>.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Is there parking at Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>Only limited parking is available on Pfaffenwaldring near Stuttgart Media University (HdM) and the University of Stuttgart. Because space is limited, we strongly recommend coming by public transport (S-Bahn or bus).</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Is there camping at Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>No, Straussi Festival does not offer camping on site. It is a day festival without overnight accommodation on the grounds. However, there are hotels, hostels and Airbnb accommodation around Vaihingen and Stuttgart.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Where exactly is the festival site?</summary>
      <p>Straussi Festival takes place on the grounds of the Straussi 1, 2 and 3 student residences at Universitätsstraße 94, 70569 Stuttgart, Germany.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Where can I find lost &amp; found at Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>Lost &amp; found is at the info point in the “Straussidreieck”, in the centre of the festival site.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Where can I find first aid at Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>The first aid tent is right next to the info point in the “Straussidreieck”, in the centre of the festival site.</p>
    </details>

    <h2>Food &amp; drinks</h2>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Is there food and drink at the festival?</summary>
      <p>Yes, Straussi Festival offers a wide range of food trucks and food stalls as well as alcoholic and non-alcoholic drinks.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Are there free drinking water stations on the festival site?</summary>
      <p>Yes, free drinking water stations are available across the whole festival site.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Can I bring my own food or drinks?</summary>
      <p>No, bringing your own food and drinks onto the festival site is not permitted.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>How can I pay on site?</summary>
      <p>Payment on the entire festival site is by card only; cash is not accepted.</p>
    </details>

    <h2>Rules &amp; safety</h2>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>What am I not allowed to bring onto the festival site?</summary>
      <p>Not allowed are, among other things, weapons of any kind, pyrotechnics, bags larger than A4, glass containers of any kind, drones, illegal drugs and bulky items (please leave the sofa at home). The full list of prohibited items will be announced.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Can I take photos or videos at Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>Private photos and videos with your phone are allowed at Straussi Festival. Professional photography and videography as well as the use of drones are not permitted anywhere on the festival site.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Is the festival site accessible?</summary>
      <p>The site is largely flat and therefore generally accessible. Some areas such as lawns or gravel paths may, however, be difficult for wheelchair users or people with reduced mobility. Details on accessible toilets, reserved areas and a contact person will be announced.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Is there an awareness team at Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>Yes, an awareness team is on duty on the festival site and can be approached in case of discrimination, harassment or other incidents. It is important to the festival to create a safe space free from racism, sexism, homophobia or any other form of discrimination. How to recognise the team, the code word and its exact location will be announced.</p>
    </details>

    <h2>Timetable &amp; site plan</h2>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Where can I find the timetable for Straussi Festival 2027?</summary>
      <p>The timetable with all performance times will be available on site during the festival weekend.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Is there a site plan for Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>Yes, the site plan will be available on site during the festival weekend.</p>
    </details>

    <h2>Social media</h2>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Is there a hashtag for Straussi Festival?</summary>
      <p>Yes, the festival's official hashtags are #straussifestival and #straussifestival2027.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-question">
      <summary>Is there a Festival A to Z besides the FAQ?</summary>
      <p>Yes, all key points about Straussi Festival are also summarised in the <a href="#abc">Festival A to Z</a>.</p>
    </details>

    <h2 id="abc">Festival A to Z</h2>
